  "details": "Description\n\nA bug has occurred where my body tilts to the left whenever I enable upper-body tracking. As a \"silent\" user (someone who does not use a microphone), I rely on this feature to express emotions, so I would greatly appreciate it if this could be fixed as soon as possible.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nPlease fix it soon—I really love it.\n\nIn the Android version of VRChat, open the settings and enable \"Enable Upper Body Tracking.\"\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: その他\n\n- Frequency: いつも\n\n---\n\nplatform: AndroidMobile (platform: Android - Mobile, store: PlayStore, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: Android\n\nclientVersion: 2026.4.2-1953-d52354d5be-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report\n\n---\n\n**Log file:** [output_log_2026-11-27_16-27-01.txt](https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/file/file_20ee41dc-2afb-4578-a3bd-9e5dac6c6fc7/1/file)",
